WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:09.006
This is OpsFlow Agent, an operations copilot for understanding text, finding demo
employee policies, drafting emails and scheduling reminders.

00:00:09.006 --> 00:00:13.378
This is a real browser recording with live model responses.

00:00:13.378 --> 00:00:19.935
We will try three requests, inspect the tools in Activity, and return to saved
results.

00:00:21.979 --> 00:00:23.880
First, a policy question.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.159
OpsFlow searches a local collection of fictional employee policies.

00:00:28.159 --> 00:00:32.437
These are demonstration policies, not a real employer’s rules.

00:00:38.836 --> 00:00:44.795
Activity shows the work as it happens: classification, routing, model calls and
tool execution.

00:00:44.795 --> 00:00:48.626
The answer appears after the outcome has been saved.

00:00:59.684 --> 00:01:03.384
The answer is based on the matching remote work policy.

00:01:03.384 --> 00:01:11.153
Activity keeps the exact retrieval result, the selected route and elapsed time, so
we can inspect the evidence behind the explanation.

00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:19.766
Opening Activity reveals the workflow and tool records.

00:01:19.766 --> 00:01:23.684
This is observable execution data, not private model reasoning.

00:01:23.684 --> 00:01:27.602
The policy answer remains marked as fictional demo information.

00:01:31.537 --> 00:01:34.015
Second, one request with four operations.

00:01:34.015 --> 00:01:41.449
We will analyze a complaint, extract its keywords, summarize the incident, and
draft a professional email to Alex.

00:01:41.449 --> 00:01:45.992
The agent can choose tools in sequence and use their results.

00:01:51.714 --> 00:01:57.673
Activity shows the work as it happens: classification, routing, model calls and
tool execution.

00:01:57.673 --> 00:02:01.504
The answer appears after the outcome has been saved.

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:31.067
The completed response brings the analysis and draft together.

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:36.394
The draft has a recipient, subject and body, followed by separate review
instructions.

00:02:36.394 --> 00:02:39.672
Creating this draft has not sent an email.

00:02:44.154 --> 00:02:51.347
Activity records the tools that actually ran: sentiment analysis, keyword
extraction, summarization and email drafting.

00:02:51.347 --> 00:02:55.183
Each tool has saved arguments, results and timing.

00:02:55.183 --> 00:03:00.458
Earlier successful results would remain available if a later operation failed.

00:03:17.716 --> 00:03:19.363
Third, a follow-up reminder.

00:03:19.363 --> 00:03:24.305
We supply one task, a date, a clear time and a timezone.

00:03:24.305 --> 00:03:28.836
Reminder requests always use the agent, with local validation before storage.

00:03:36.706 --> 00:03:42.665
Activity shows the work as it happens: classification, routing, model calls and
tool execution.

00:03:42.665 --> 00:03:46.496
The answer appears after the outcome has been saved.

00:03:50.623 --> 00:03:54.690
The acknowledgement shows the stored task and exact resolved due time.

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:56.538
Scheduling writes a reminder record.

00:03:56.538 --> 00:03:59.865
It does not send an email or start delivery.

00:03:59.865 --> 00:04:02.823
This recording leaves the separate reminder worker stopped.

00:04:06.752 --> 00:04:12.077
Settings, Reminders shows the task, its recorded timezone and current delivery
state.

00:04:12.077 --> 00:04:13.852
Refresh only reads storage.

00:04:13.852 --> 00:04:20.952
A scheduled state means delivery is still pending; even SMTP acceptance would not
prove inbox arrival.

00:04:25.363 --> 00:04:28.645
Settings, Emails collects successful drafts across saved chats.

00:04:28.645 --> 00:04:34.799
Here is the draft from our complaint example, with its source conversation and
review actions.

00:04:34.799 --> 00:04:38.901
Opening this page does not draft again or send anything.

00:04:47.065 --> 00:04:50.177
Evaluations separates classifier performance from generation quality.

00:04:50.177 --> 00:04:55.067
The recorded classifier accuracy is eighty-eight percent on a synthetic holdout.

00:04:55.067 --> 00:05:01.290
These saved results are historical evidence; opening the page does not rerun the
model.

00:05:06.131 --> 00:05:11.991
The generation table is an automated review of five available answers from eight
planned examples.

00:05:11.991 --> 00:05:15.117
Ratings use a zero-to-three scale with explicit counts.

00:05:15.117 --> 00:05:20.978
This small development sample is not an overall agent accuracy or an independent
human benchmark.

00:05:27.741 --> 00:05:34.036
Refreshing restores the saved conversation and its Activity without submitting the
request again.

00:05:34.036 --> 00:05:43.236
OpsFlow connects natural language to inspectable tools, keeps the results, and
distinguishes analysis, drafts, scheduled work and actual delivery.

00:05:43.236 --> 00:05:47.109
Review the README for setup, architecture and limitations.
